[pulsewasm:providers] fastly-native-platform-capabilities
[pulsewasm] Fastly Config, Secret, KV, and GRIP capabilities (timeout 300.00s)
ok - repeated config effect handoff preserves site identities, order, missing values, errors, and cancellation
ok - Fastly Native shares a total request budget across KV operations and blocks the checkpoint
ok - Fastly deadline preserves remote acceptance uncertainty
ok - Fastly final response write is fenced; completed handoff is not withdrawn
ok - Fastly body admission, invalid clocks, stale artifacts and JS rejection are bounded
ok - Fastly budget starts at request entry, before ABI setup
ok - Fastly outbound preparation cannot dispatch fetch after expiry
ok - shared error-driver settlement preserves the fatal-return deadline fence and transport diagnostics
ok - bounded Fastly concatenation preserves snapshots, UTF-16 and exact digest bytes; memory 8650752
ok - scalar-heavy Fastly schema encoding preserves exact escaped bytes and independent collections; memory 115343360
ok - Fastly scalar sharing preserves numeric bounds, distinct enums, nested projections, optionality, errors and generation isolation
ok - Fastly structural code sharing: 86 semantic controls, fresh projections, alias isolation and frozen decoded values
ok - MEM01 instrumentation is isolated, anchored and allocator accounting balances
ok - explicit Fastly text encode preserves exact bytes, Unicode, projection, alias mutation, admission and pre-effect failures
ok - O-05 101 parser cases preserve text, errors, scalar identity and owned storage
ok - Fastly platform D2 value parity: UTF-16 ordering/indexing and exact numeric remainder
